        "content": "**Memmy Agent** is a personal AI agent and local memory hub, created on July 16, 2026. The project enables **shared memory across multiple AI agents** including Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw, and Hermes Agent, solving the problem of context loss when switching between different AI assistants.\n\nThe system provides a **MemOS-powered memory engine** that automatically collects and structures user knowledge, preferences, and work experience into \"searchable, reusable long-term memory.\" Memmy offers **three core capabilities**:\n\n1. A **cross-agent memory layer** that imports historical conversations from existing agents\n2. A **local agent runtime** supporting desktop app, CLI/TUI, and OpenAI-compatible API interfaces\n3. **Tool integration** through MCP and custom Skills for external platforms like Telegram, Discord, GitHub, and Slack\n\nThe project follows a **local-first architecture** where memory and configuration are stored on the user's machine. It's licensed under MIT and has accumulated 525 GitHub stars and 53 forks. The full stack runs on Node.js 22+ with a single-command startup process via `scripts/dev-start.sh`."
