        "content": "# VulnHunter Project Overview\n\n**Creation & Repository Details:**\nVulnHunter was created on July 7, 2026, by Capital One and is publicly hosted on GitHub under the Apache License 2.0.\n\n**What It Does:**\nVulnHunter operates as an \"agentic AI security tool\" that employs an \"attacker-first analysis\" methodology for source code review. Rather than using conventional pattern-matching techniques common in static analysis tools, it simulates how an adversary would approach a codebase.\n\nThe tool follows a three-stage workflow:\n\n1. **Hunt** (`/vulnhunt`): Maps entry points to dangerous operations and validates findings through a \"multi-stage falsification pipeline\" to reduce false positives\n\n2. **Fix** (`/vulnhunter-fix`): Creates test cases, implements remediation code, and generates pull requests for verified vulnerabilities\n\n3. **Verify** (`/vulnhunt-fix-verify`): Independently confirms that fixes successfully address identified security issues\n\n**Key Differentiators:**\nVulnHunter uses \"forward analysis\" starting from potential entry points rather than backward analysis from dangerous functions. It incorporates a reasoning framework designed to challenge its own findings before reporting them.\n\n**Technical Requirements:**\nThe system requires Claude Code CLI with access to the Opus model, plus Python 3.12+ for automation components. Users must provide their own model credentials."
