      {
        "tool_use_id": "call_9e56be0159384618826e1c20",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "# KlaatCode: Terminal AI Coding Agent\n\n## Project Overview\nKlaatCode is an open-source terminal-native AI coding agent developed by KlaatAI, positioned as a cost-efficient alternative to tools like Claude Code, Cursor, and opencode. It leverages \"Klaatu-o1,\" a smart routing model that automatically selects the appropriate AI model tier for each task.\n\n## Key Features\n- **Smart Model Routing**: Automatically routes requests through five cost tiers (nano, fast, code, reason, heavy) to optimize costs while maintaining frontier-level accuracy when needed\n- **Code Knowledge Graph**: Uses semantic search and call graph analysis instead of basic grep, reducing token usage by 5–15×\n- **Unlimited Tool Rounds**: No \"Continue\" button interruptions—tool calls don't count against quota, only user messages do\n- **Real-time Cost Monitoring**: Burn-rate warnings, per-task cost attribution, and hard session caps to prevent runaway spending\n- **Context Management**: Smart compaction that verifies summaries don't lose critical information, with explicit recovery guidance if something is dropped\n- **Terminal UI**: Syntax-highlighted markdown responses, 14 themes, mouse support, and vim keybindings\n- **Multi-Agent Workflows**: Delegate scoped work to sub-agents that can run in parallel\n\n## Benchmark Results\nBased on 33-task benchmark (2026-07-20):\n- **Solve rate**: 33/33 tasks (perfect)\n- **Cost**: $0.027 per solved task (5.4× cheaper than Claude Code's $0.146)\n- **Tokens**: 51.7K per solved task (3.3× fewer than Claude's 171.5K)\n- **Speed**: 23s median time per task\n\n## Installation\nAvailable via npm, one-line installers, Homebrew, and building from source. Requires Node ≥18 or Bun ≥1 for installation, but produces a standalone binary.\n\n## Repository\nThe project is hosted on GitHub at `KlaatAI/klaatcode` under the Apache 2.0 license and has 353 stars and 137 forks."
      }
    ]
  },
