        "content": "# OpenHub Project Overview\n\n**Project:** OpenHub by 24KaratAu\n\n**Creation Date:** July 23, 2026\n\n**What it does:** OpenHub is a \"keyboard-first, terminal user interface (TUI) discovery hub and package installer for AI coding tools, skills, and agents.\" Built using Python, Textual, and SQLite, the application serves as a centralized catalog and manager for AI development tools.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- Dashboard interface showing trending repositories, releases, and tools\n- Fuzzy search functionality with typo tolerance\n- Curated collections for different use cases (AI Engineer Starter Pack, Claude Desktop Servers, etc.)\n- Universal skill export compatible with multiple AI coding environments\n- Background synchronization with GitHub data\n- Activity logging for all installations and exports\n\n## Ecosystem Compatibility\n\nThe tool exports packages using the \"Universal Open Agent Skills Standard (SKILL.md),\" making them compatible with:\n- OpenCode\n- Claude Code/Desktop\n- Cursor Editor\n- Windsurf/Cascade\n- Roo Code/Cline\n- AutoGen/CrewAI\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python 3.10 or higher\n- Works on Linux, macOS, and Windows (PowerShell/Windows Terminal)\n\n## Installation\n\nAvailable via pipx, pip, or local development clone. The application appears to be open source with MIT licensing."
