        "content": "Based on the GitHub repository content:\n\n**Project Details:**\nBossConsole (BOSS) is an Apache-2.0 licensed open-source desktop application that bills itself as \"the operator's console for AI agents.\" It's built with Kotlin Multiplatform and Compose Multiplatform, running natively on the JVM rather than Electron.\n\n**Creation Status:**\nThe repository shows 96 commits and is actively maintained by risa-labs-inc. The latest release version is available through the BossConsole-Releases repository.\n\n**Core Purpose:**\nThe application serves as a multi-platform harness for running AI coding agents like Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, and OpenCode. It provides these agents with real tools including an embedded browser, terminal, code editor, secrets management, and automation capabilities through the Model Context Protocol (MCP).\n\n**Key Distinctions:**\nThe platform emphasizes its multi-threaded JVM architecture, hot-reload plugin system, and governance features including role-based access control and per-tool kill switches. It supports macOS, Windows, and Linux across both x64 and ARM64 architectures.\n\nThe project includes roughly 100+ MCP tools across approximately 20 plugins and positions itself as an alternative to closed-source AI agent desktop environments."
