        "content": "# AgentDoctor Project Overview\n\n## Basic Information\n- **Repository**: pranee54/AgentDoctor\n- **Creation Date**: July 28, 2026\n- **License**: MIT\n- **Status**: Public beta (v0.2.0-beta)\n- **Language**: TypeScript/Node.js\n\n## What It Does\nAgentDoctor is a local CLI tool that functions as a \"Lighthouse for AI coding agents.\" It performs static analysis audits of project-level AI coding agent configurations across Cursor, Claude Code, and Codex environments.\n\n## Key Features\n- Scans for security vulnerabilities (exposed environment files, private keys)\n- Analyzes MCP (Model Context Protocol) filesystem scopes\n- Checks instruction file configurations\n- Identifies context waste (large logs, generated directories)\n- Provides deterministic findings with stable rule IDs\n- No API key required and no code upload by default\n\n## How It Works\nThe tool inspects repository files such as `.cursor/rules`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`, and `.mcp.json` to identify potential security and configuration issues before they become repository problems.\n\n## Installation\nRun directly via npx: `npx @praneeth_54/agentdoctor`\n\nRequires Node.js 20+.\n\nThe README emphasizes that AgentDoctor \"analyzes configuration. It does not run agents, call an LLM, or modify your repository in this release.\""
